WEBVTT

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:03.507
Now let's rank employees within each department.

00:00:03.507 --> 00:00:07.647
The RANK window function calculates a position inside each department.

00:00:07.647 --> 00:00:14.927
PARTITION BY restarts the ranking for each department, and ORDER BY salary descending makes the highest salary

00:00:14.927 --> 00:00:17.902
rank first. Run the query and inspect the department boundaries.

00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:21.092
You should see rank one appear separately in each department.

00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:23.962
Notice that every employee row remains visible.

00:00:23.962 --> 00:00:27.037
That is the major difference from a grouped salary report.

00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:32.417
If two employees have the same salary, RANK can produce ties and skip the next rank number.

00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:38.982
That behavior is useful to remember when comparing RANK with other ranking functions such as DENSE_RANK or

00:00:38.982 --> 00:00:43.187
ROW_NUMBER. Window functions calculate across related rows without collapsing them.

00:00:43.187 --> 00:00:48.522
That lets you keep row-level detail while adding rank, running totals, or group averages.

00:00:48.522 --> 00:00:54.752
Always define the partition and ordering carefully because those clauses describe which rows belong together

00:00:54.752 --> 00:00:55.896
and in what sequence.
